Z||000000||Taijiguy||07-13-2000||10:36 AM||||It suddenly occurred to me that there seem to be fairly large number of members located relatively close to one another. I notice alot of guys (and/or gals) who seem to be located in the central Ohio (Columbus) area for example. Has anyone ever considered the prospect of holding a number of individual local gatherings?<BR>I for one would love the opportunity to meet and cultivate friendships with the people who are local to me.<BR>I'd be willing to work on coordinating one here in Central Ohio if anyone else in the area shares my interest. <BR>How about some feedback on this....<P>-Taiji<P>||||reg||10
Z||000001||lennyb4||07-13-2000||10:47 AM||||If your in Ohio i know alot of us would like to get together. I just wish there were some poeple on here from the cleveland area. Most of the Ohio people are from the southern area's. But if you get a chance some of us are getting together at Norwalk Raceway this August at the Pontiac Nationals or something like that. Im sure one of the other guys will be able to give you (and remind me) of the actual dates.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smallPegasus.gif">  <BR>87 Coupe... Got rice???||||reg||1
Z||000002||2M4 Dale||07-13-2000||11:38 AM||||Go to search and type in Cookout and Drags. You'll see the posting for the August AMFC event. The more the merrier!!!||||reg||6
Z||000003||87ECO5||07-13-2000||12:42 PM||||Ya, the people here in the Indiana, Kentucky and Ohio area are pretty active.  We average one big outing per month (some of us hang out every weekend or so).<P>We've got a big ring of friends known unofficially as SOAPOIFOG (Southern Ohio And Part Of Indiana Fiero Owners Group       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   ) or the IndiOhio group.  It consists of <B>Monkeyman</B> and <B>BOILERMAKER</B> from Indiana, <B>tgowens</B> from Kentucky, and <B>2M4 Dale</B>, <B>ChadMan</B>, <B>fiero56</B>, <B>william_thorniii</B>, <B>BENGAL4</B>, <B>redfiero</B>, <B>FieroWife</B> (my wife, Lisa) and myself (<B>87ECsomething</B>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   ) - all from Ohio.  There are several others but we're the ones that just about live together!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>There are several outings going on as both lennyb4 and 2M4 Dale mentioned:<P><B>JULY</B> - Later this month (7/27-7/30), most of us are heading to Louisville for the annual Fiero Nationals.  Some of us are hooking up with the big C.O.F.E. caravan that's originating in Columbus.<P><B>AUGUST</B> - We're having a big (two day - 8/12 and 8/13) outing at 2M4 Dale's place.  On 8/12, we're doing a bunch of stuff, including cooking out and camping out at his place.  On 8/13, we're cruising to Norwalk Raceway for the Pontiac Nationals.<P><B>SEPTEMBER</B> - Since I haven't organized anything since June, I believe I'll be hosting something at my place (or nearby) in late September.  Probably another cruise like a few of us did earlier this year (February, I think) where we ate breakfast then cruised on some nice (and icy!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">   ) roads through the Fort Ancient State Park area.  A certain member will have his S/C 3800 back by then and I can't think of a better thing to do than get out of the city limits and allow him to open it up!     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><B>OCTOBER</B> - We've got a big bash scheduled to celebrate several of our birthdays.<P>BTW, as most of the guys will acknowledge, my house has taken on an open door policy!  If you're ever in the area, you're more than welcome to stop in.  FieroWife loves these cars as much as (if not more than) I do and she's <B>VERY</B> generous with allowing me "Fiero Time".  I'm the luckiest man in the world!!!!!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Stick around, Taijiguy!  We're just getting started!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 07-13-2000).]||||reg||14
